 "web": "These barriers land on the same household at once. One older homeowner: the roof she has patched for years finally fails (1); a 311 complaint brings a 30-day notice (2); her tax bill rose in 2023 while her Social Security check did not (3); the bank was never generous with this side of town (4); a cash buyer slips a card in her door offering to take the house as is (5); her neighbor who would help translates the city's letter for her own parents (6); her son, who could do the roofing, works cash jobs with no sick days (7); the deed is still in her late husband's name, so the city program asks for papers she doesn't have (9); and the bank's smallest repair loan is $10,000 against her house, while a payday lender will hand her $300 today (10). No one barrier decides whether she stays in her house. Together they set the price.",
